.TH ACME-MATERIALIZE 1 "2026-08-18" "rgbdns 0.6.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
acme-materialize \- merge durable ACME DNS-01 state into tinydns source
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B acme-materialize
.I data acme-config state-directory output
.SH DESCRIPTION
Validates the scoped ACME update configuration and durable overlay, applies
challenge TXT values and monotonic SOA serials to the source zone, and writes
the merged tinydns snapshot atomically. It is a non-networked publication
stage intended to precede ANAME materialization and DNSSEC signing.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero on success, 100 for usage errors, and 111 for operational failures.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR rgbdns-acme (1),
.BR aname-materialize (1),
.BR dnssec-sign (1)
